      "slug": "glass-noodles",
      "term": "Glass Noodles",
      "definition": "Thin noodles made from mung bean or sweet potato starch that turn translucent when cooked. They have a slippery, springy texture and absorb surrounding flavours well. Also called cellophane noodles or bean thread noodles."
    },
    {
      "slug": "doubanjiang",
      "term": "Doubanjiang",
      "definition": "A fermented paste made from broad beans and chillies, central to Sichuan cooking. It is salty, spicy and deeply savoury. Pixian county doubanjiang is considered the finest variety."
    },
    {
      "slug": "shaoxing-wine",
      "term": "Shaoxing Wine",
      "definition": "A Chinese rice wine with a nutty, amber flavour used widely in marinades, sauces and braises. Named after the city of Shaoxing in Zhejiang province. Dry sherry is the closest substitute."
    }
  ],
