  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This Sichuan staple comes together in about 30 minutes and serves 4."
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Glass noodles",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "glass-noodles"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "are soaked until pliable, then simmered in a sauce built on"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "doubanjiang",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "doubanjiang"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "and"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Shaoxing wine",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "shaoxing-wine"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The pork mince catches in the noodle strands, giving the dish its famous name."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use scissors to cut the soaked noodles into 15 cm lengths before cooking. Long strands tangle badly in the wok and are hard to serve."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
